So `update_branch` fires for BEHIND PRs (silent-update-behind) and for parked PRs (park-reset — the head-change RESET probe). A PR parked with `validation_failed` continues to route through update_branch via the park-reset rule. So after the workflows-park, the next tick will again attempt silent-update → rejection → escalation → rejection → "park" attempt again (guarded by labels snapshot → no second comment) — but that means the escalation push is attempted every tick. That's "self-healing" in the same way as the existing trail — if the App later gains Workflows: write, the escalated push succeeds and the head moves → park clears (gh-994 head-change reset). Good.

But "one marker, no infinite retries" for E1: the distinct marker should be posted once (deduped). The existing park comment dedupe works via the labels snapshot: `if ((ticket.labels || []).indexOf('validation_failed') === -1)`. Since the park posts `parked-head: <sha>` and the escalation park should also record the parked-head, a subsequent successful escalation moves the head and the gh-994 RESET clears the park (AC4). 

So design in smAgent fork path:

```js
function forkSilentUpdateBranchTracked(branchName, forkFull) {
   var stderrFile = silentUpdateStderrFile(branchName);
   try {
       forkSilentUpdateBranch(branchName, forkFull, stderrFile);
       return;
   } catch (eFork) {
       var tail = readSilentUpdateStderrTail(stderrFile);
       if (validationLivenessModule.isWorkflowsPermissionRejection(tail)) {
           // gh-1106 AC1/AC2: the rejection is a token-capability fact —
           // escalate once with the workflow-write token, never counted
           // on the gh-1070 trail.
           if (escalateForkSilentUpdate(branchName, forkFull, stderrFile)) return; // head moved
           throw silentUpdateErrorWithTail(eFork, tail);
       }
       recordForkSilentUpdateFailure(validationLivenessModule.silentUpdateRejectionReason(tail));
       throw silentUpdateErrorWithTail(eFork, tail);
