Confirmed: the real content is `'https://x-access-token:[REDACTED:Connection String Password]@github.com/'` — my tool output redacts `x-access-token:${GH_TOKEN}` as `[REDACTED:Connection String Password]` (sandbox display-layer redaction). So:

1. When I READ code containing the contiguous token-URL, I see `[REDACTED:...]`.
2. When I WRITE code containing it, it would also get mangled — so I must use split literals in any new source (like smAgent does: `'https://x-access-' + 'token:${GH_TOKEN}@github.com/'`).

For my changes, I don't need to write any new token-URL — the escalation reuses `silentUpdateCommand` with the same pushTarget (`forkPushTokenUrl(forkFull)`). In validationLiveness, I only add the classifier (regexes) and maybe a marker-line builder — no token URLs. In smProvider, no URL literals either ('gh pr update-branch ...'). Good.

Test fixtures will need the rejection phrases — those contain no tokens. For asserting push URLs in tests, use the TOK split convention.

Now — the `REG-1` requirement: "existing gh-1070 / gh-1074 fork tests unchanged and green". My changes must not alter the chain bytes for non-workflows failures.

Let me also double-check `machine-sm.yml`/`factory-sm.yml` deliver sourceToken (the ticket says they already do; non-goal to change them). RUN_JOB_PARAMS.sourceToken — how is it populated? factory-sm.yml (in the external workflows repo) maps SOURCE_GITHUB_TOKEN secret → sourceToken param. In this repo, machine-sm.yml passes secrets SOURCE_GITHUB_TOKEN / APP_ID / APP_PRIVATE_KEY to the reusable factory-sm.yml. So `jobParams.sourceToken` exists at runtime. Good — the escalation reads `(RUN_JOB_PARAMS || {}).sourceToken`.

Now the marker/park wording. Distinct reason naming the missing token capability:

Park comment (via a new poster, NOT parkForkGuest — parkForkGuest's reason text says "maintainer edits"; I need distinct):

```js
function parkForkWorkflowWrite(reason) {
   // gh-1106 AC3 ...
   if (parkedRedHeadThisPass) return;
   var tracker = githubTracker(...);
   if ((ticket.labels || []).indexOf('validation_failed') === -1) {
       tracker.addLabel(ticket.prNumber, 'validation_failed');
   }
   var head = resolveHeadSha(effectiveRepoInfo, ticket) || 'unknown';
   tracker.postComment(ticket.prNumber,
       '🛑 validation_failed — fork park (gh-1106): ' + reason +
       ' A workflow-capable token (App installation token with "Workflows: write", or a PAT with the `workflow` scope) as `sourceToken` lets the machine finish the update; ANY head-moving push (including a later successful escalation) clears this park automatically. parked-head: ' + head);
}
``

Marker: the ticket says "parks with a distinct reason/marker". I'll include a distinct marker line so greps/dedupes work:

Actually — keep it simple: the park comment IS the marker (like recordNoRefBookeeping's parkBody includes the triggerFailMarkerLine). I'll define in validationLiveness:

```js
// gh-1106: the distinct workflow-write park marker — NOT a 3-strike
// silent-update failure marker (never counted on that trail).
function workflowWriteParkLine(headSha, atIso) {
   return '🔐 workflow-write park (gh-1106) — update needs a workflow-write token at ' + (atIso || '') + ' · parked-head: ' + headSha;
}
``

Hmm, wait. Let me re-read AC3: "if escalation also fails with the same class, the PR parks with a distinct reason/marker naming the missing token capability (UT-3)." And the architecture diagram: "park with a DISTINCT reason 'update needs workflow-write token' (actionable, not 'edits revoked'); not counted toward the 3-strike trail".

And AC4: "after a successful escalated push the `validation_failed` hold is released by the existing 'new push since park' rule and CI is dispatched (IT-2)". The existing release path = gh-994 head-change reset (park comment records parked-head: <sha>; the head moves later → next tick's update_branch RESET removes the label). So my park comment MUST record `parked-head: <sha>`. IT-2 test: escalate success → head moves → next tick park cleared. That's the existing reset — nothing new to implement, but I need to ensure the park comment records the sha (postForkParkComment-style).

Decision: reuse `postForkParkComment(reason)` + label add — i.e., call `parkForkGuest(distinctReason)`? parkForkGuest's guard `parkedRedHeadThisPass` is desirable. The reason text differs. parkForkGuest posts: '🛑 validation_failed — fork park (gh-1070): ' + reason + ' Update the branch from main ... parked-head: ...'. The prefix says gh-1070 — for distinctness I'd rather have a gh-1106 prefix. I'll write a separate poster miroring parkForkGuest but with the gh-1106 wording. Two similar functions — acceptable (the codebase splits parkNonEditableFork similarly for guards).

Comment dedupe across ticks: guard on the label snapshot — only post when `(ticket.labels||[]).indexOf('validation_failed') === -1`? But the live #1591 case is ALREADY parked (label present in snapshot) — the first gh-1106 tick would post nothing... but the escalation would still be attempted (the retry) and succeed → head moves → park clears (gh-994). If the escalation also fails → silent hold, no comment. Hmm, that leaves the PR parked with the OLD (wrong "edits revoked") comment and no gh-1106 marker naming the real reason. That's a real timeline gap for exactly the live case the ticket cites.

Better: dedupe on the parked-head sha — post the gh-1106 marker only if no existing comment carries `workflow-write park (gh-1106)` AND `parked-head: <current head>`. Reads PR comments once (github_get_pr_comments) — the same pattern as recordNoRefBookeeping/ghost-guard audit. This gives: live #1591 (parked, old comment) → first gh-1106 tick posts the distinct marker once (even though label already present); subsequent ticks (same head, marker present) post nothing. If the head later moves (author push), park clears anyway via gh-994.

Wait, but if the head moved and the silent push is now rejected AGAIN for workflows (new workflow change in main), a new marker for the new head would post — correct.

But hold on — if the escalation FAILS with the same class, should we park even when `validation_failed` is already present? The label add is guarded (idempotent), the comment deduped by head. Fine.

