   try {
       forkSilentUpdateBranch(branchName, forkFull, escStderrFile);
       return true; // moved
   } finally {
       if (swapped) { try { set_env_variable('GH_TOKEN', silentTok); } catch (eRes) {} }
   }
} catch (eEsc) { ... }
``

Wait — but if silentToken is absent from jobParams (yet ambient GH_TOKEN was the silent github.token — the machine-sm.yml wiring passes silent-token separately from jobParams... hmm, actually `silent-token: ${{ github.token }}` is a workflow INPUT; the factory maps it into jobParams.silentToken presumably, AND/OR the env). If jobParams.silentToken is missing but ambient is still the workflow token, then not swapping env would push with the ambient token again (rejected). The escalation NEEDS the env swap to sourceToken regardless. Restore: without silentToken, restore to... we can't know. But AC7: "GH_TOKEN env is restored after escalation even on exception". The existing precedent (stampValidationChecksForModule) only restores when it swapped AND the restore token is known. If silentToken is unknown, the best-effort restore is sourceToken (same as the ambient assumption in the other swaps — ambient is the source PAT). I'll restore to `silentTok || sourceTok`... no wait, that leaves the env on sourceTok — matching the codebase-wide ambient assumption ("restore after (sourceToken)"). That's exactly what every other swap site does: restore to sourceToken unconditionally. 

Decision (codebase-consistent): 
- swap in sourceToken before the escalated chain;
- finally: restore `set_env_variable('GH_TOKEN', silentTok || sourceTok)` — hmm, but every other site restores to sourceTok only. The silent chain that runs BEFORE the escalation uses ambient. If ambient were sourceToken, the silent push would fire CI and would NOT be silent... but the ticket asserts the silent push uses silentToken=github.token. In the live deployment, GH_TOKEN env for the SM job = github.token (silent) — that's how the silent push is silent. And the other swap sites restore to sourceTok — leaving the AMBIENT as sourceTok for later ops?! That would make subsequent silent pushes NON-silent... 

