A flaky test: the UT-1 assertion compares `pushOf(cmd2) === pushOf(cmd1)` where pushOf takes everything from 'git push ' to the END — which includes the stderr-tee suffix containing `Date.now()`-based paths. The two attempts run in different milliseconds → different dir names → flaky failure. It passed in the earlier run (same-ms timing) and failed here.

Fix the test: compare only the push TARGET (from 'git push ' up to the ' 2>' / '; }' suffix), not the whole tail. Extract up to '.git HEAD:<branch>' — use the substring from 'git push ' to the first '; } 2>>' or compare a slice ending at 'HEAD:' + BRANCH.

Better: assert both commands CONTAIN the identical fork push target string, and that cmd2's chain ends with the same 'HEAD:<branch>' segment. Simplest robust: 

```js
var targetOf = function (c) {
   var start = c.indexOf('git push ');
   var end = c.indexOf('.git ', start);
   return c.slice(start, end + 4) + ' + BRANCH...
};
``

Hmm, the push target in the chain: 'git push https://x-access-token:[REDACTED:Connection String Password]@github.com/YuryBY/dmtools-dart.git HEAD:fix/android-dap-home-sandbox'. The stderr tee follows AFTER '; } 2>>...'. So slice from 'git push ' to the first '; }' occurrence:

```js
var pushOf = function (c) {
   var start = c.indexOf('git push ');
   var end = c.indexOf('; } 2>>', start);
   return c.slice(start, end === -1 ? undefined : end);
};
``

That yields 'git push <url> HEAD:<branch>' for both — identical. Fix and re-run the smAgent suite; then a final full re-run.

